 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "100:1-6 addresses the Prophet ﷺ: no plate there. A falling leaf for «منها قائم وحصيد» (no ruins drawn). Geometric for «وكذلك أخذ ربك», an hourglass for «لأجل معدود». The Gathering (103) is never drawn: no crowd. The plan's «أنباء القرى» was a passage pair. 100:1-6 avoids As-Sa'di's «وموعظة وذكرى للمؤمنين» (11:120 wording). STAGING v4: c1 (100-101): the towns whose people were destroyed, shown as an empty town by day (no person on stage). 100:1-6 is addressed to the Prophet: the camera only, no plate there and no speaker. A leaf plate for some still standing and some mown down (100:7-9), and the ruin event on 100:9 (As-Sa'di: their dwellings fell and no trace was left); the town stays in ruins through 101. Their gods are never drawn and nothing turns toward an empty side (101:7-16: the camera holds wide); geometric for when the command of your Lord came (101:18-20). c2 (102-104) stays ambient (geometric): Allah's seizing of the towns is His act told directly, and 103-104 are the Hereafter, the Day all people are gathered to (never drawn: no crowd); params.quiet over all of 102-104 so no pulse reads as a voice or a presence. Plates: geometric for the seizure of your Lord (102:1-8), an hourglass for a term counted (104:4-5). Cover: the empty, ruined town (where the wrongdoers fell)."
